# Modern C++

Write C++17, not C with a `.cpp` extension. Keep files small (structs + functions). Do not add frameworks.

## Constants

- `inline constexpr` (in a header) or `constexpr` (in a .cpp). No `#define` for numbers or strings.
- Shared tunables live in `namespace hh` in `game_constants.hpp` as ALL_CAPS `inline constexpr` (see naming-conventions).
- Magic numbers in a `.cpp` become named `constexpr` values (camelCase locals, ALL_CAPS if they belong in `game_constants.hpp`).

```cpp
// BAD
#define WINDOW_WIDTH 1280
InitWindow(WINDOW_WIDTH, 720, "Heart House");

// GOOD
namespace hh {
inline constexpr int WINDOW_WIDTH = 1280;
inline constexpr int WINDOW_HEIGHT = 720;
}
InitWindow(hh::WINDOW_WIDTH, hh::WINDOW_HEIGHT, "Heart House");
```

## Language

- `nullptr`, not `NULL` or `0` for pointers.
- `[[nodiscard]]` on functions whose return value must not be ignored (init, queries).
- Range-for when looping a known container. `auto` when the type is obvious and noisy.
- `std::array` / `std::string_view` over C arrays and raw `const char*` when it does not fight Raylib/Steam (they still want `const char*` at the call).
- `#pragma once` in headers.

Do not invent classes, smart-pointer graphs, or exceptions for this game unless asked.
